        "raisedBy": [
          "privacy"
        ],
        "recommendation": "The local-part class is ASCII-only and omits characters RFC 5321/6531 allow (accented letters, ' & ! # = ? etc.). `logInfo(\"from josé@example.org\")` cannot match at all (é sits right before @), so the full address reaches the 90-day hosting logs, against the proposal's \"masks every e-mail address\" and GDPR Art. 5(1)(c)/25; `john&jane@example.org` matches only from `jane` and logs `john&j***@example.org`, leaking part of the local part. Match the local part as any run of non-space, non-@, non-delimiter characters (Unicode-aware, `u` flag) up to the @, and likewise accept non-ASCII domains (`ada@exämple.fr` is also left unmasked); add test cases for these inputs.",
        "reported": true,
        "role": "privacy",
        "severity": "medium",
        "status": "open",
